-- חוק פיצויי פיטורים, התשכ"ג-1963 — sections 1–9, 11, 11א, 12, 13, 13ב,
-- 14, 15, 16, 29, 30 and 31: who is owed severance pay — the dismissed, the
-- employee whose employer ended, the survivors, and the resignations the law
-- counts as dismissals — after a year of continuous work and through which
-- breaks, how much, on what wage (which the regulations set and the minimum
-- wage floors), when a payment to a provident fund or a pension takes its
-- place, when a collective agreement may deny it, that a release needs
-- writing, that the State is an employer like any other, and that the law
-- takes nothing from what an agreement gives. The text is
-- laws/severance-pay-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים
-- הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: the agreements and circulars set contributions to a
-- pension fund "in place of" 72% or all of the severance pay under §14,
-- and that place is the agreement's to set (§14 itself), to the extent it
-- sets it; what is left is the employer's to pay. §12 is the floor no
-- agreement goes below (§31; the Collective Agreements Law §21), and the
-- takanon's §1.28.2 restates §§1–9, 11, 11א, 14–16 and 29–31: where a
-- restatement gives less, the law governs (the root's precedence,
-- l4/lib/precedence.l4).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT minimum_wage_law

§ `חוק פיצויי פיטורים — הזכות, השיעור, והתשלום שבא במקומם`

`why the Severance Pay Law's sections state no wage` MEANS
    `set elsewhere` "שר העבודה, בתקנות פיצויי פיטורים (חישוב הפיצויים והתפטרות שרואים אותה כפיטורים), התשכ\"ד-1964, לפי סעיף 13 לחוק פיצויי פיטורים"

§§ `1`

-- (א): one who worked a year continuously — a seasonal worker, two seasons
-- in two consecutive years — for one employer or at one workplace, and was
-- dismissed, is owed severance pay by the employer who dismissed him. A
-- season is three consecutive months of a year in which he worked at
-- least 60 days. (ב): moved between workplaces of the same employer where
-- the employers changed, he is owed severance by the earlier employer for
-- his time with it, as if dismissed on the change — unless the new one
-- took that on in writing toward him, and then the earlier is released and
-- the time counts as worked at the new workplace.
@ref law:1
GIVEN `years worked continuously` IS A NUMBER
      `a seasonal worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `seasons worked in two consecutive years` IS A NUMBER
      `dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1 of the Severance Pay Law entitles him` `years worked continuously` `a seasonal worker` `seasons worked in two consecutive years` `dismissed` IF
        `dismissed`
    AND (    `years worked continuously` AT LEAST 1
         OR (`a seasonal worker` AND `seasons worked in two consecutive years` AT LEAST 2))

GIVEN `the new employer took it on in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the earlier employer owes severance for its time under section 1(ב)` `the new employer took it on in writing` IF
    NOT `the new employer took it on in writing`

#ASSERT `section 1 of the Severance Pay Law entitles him` 1 FALSE 0 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 1 of the Severance Pay Law entitles him` 0.9 FALSE 0 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 1 of the Severance Pay Law entitles him` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE
#ASSERT `section 1 of the Severance Pay Law entitles him` 0.5 TRUE 2 TRUE

§§ `2`

-- For §1, the work is continuous though it was broken off by: (1) military
-- or partial service under the Discharged Soldiers (Return to Work) Law,
-- save full service under a career undertaking that failed §1(ד) of that
-- law's conditions, and reserve duty; (2) the weekly rest, a holiday not
-- worked, and 1 May; (3) annual leave; (4) leave or recess with pay, by law
-- or with the employer's consent; (5) the same without pay; (6) a strike or
-- a lockout; (7) an accident or an illness; (8) days of mourning not worked;
-- (9) a temporary break that does not sever the relationship, or a break
-- that severs it of no more than six months; (10) training for emergency
-- labour service.
@ref law:2
DECLARE `break in work under section 2` IS ONE OF
    `military, partial or reserve service, under section 2`
    `full career service that failed its conditions, under section 2`
    `the weekly rest, a holiday not worked or 1 May, under section 2`
    `annual leave, under section 2`
    `leave or recess with pay, under section 2`
    `leave or recess without pay, under section 2`
    `a strike or a lockout, under section 2`
    `an accident or an illness, under section 2`
    `days of mourning not worked, under section 2`
    `a temporary break that does not sever the relationship, under section 2`
    `a break that severs the relationship, under section 2`
    `training for emergency labour service, under section 2`
    `another break, under section 2`

GIVEN b IS A `break in work under section 2`
      `months of the break` IS A NUMBER @desc counted for a break that severs the relationship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 2 keeps the work continuous through` b `months of the break` IF
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN `full career service that failed its conditions, under section 2` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a break that severs the relationship, under section 2` THEN `months of the break` AT MOST 6
    WHEN `another break, under section 2` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

#ASSERT `section 2 keeps the work continuous through` `a break that severs the relationship, under section 2` 6
#ASSERT NOT `section 2 keeps the work continuous through` `a break that severs the relationship, under section 2` 7
#ASSERT `section 2 keeps the work continuous through` `leave or recess without pay, under section 2` 0

§§ `3`

-- A dismissal near the end of the first year of work is taken, unless the
-- contrary is proved, as made to avoid severance, and takes nothing from
-- the right to it.
@ref law:3
GIVEN `dismissed near the end of the first year of work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary was proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 keeps the right of one dismissed near the end of his first year` `dismissed near the end of the first year of work` `the contrary was proved` IF
    `dismissed near the end of the first year of work` AND (NOT `the contrary was proved`)

#ASSERT `section 3 keeps the right of one dismissed near the end of his first year` TRUE FALSE

§§ `4`

-- One whose work stopped because his employer died or went bankrupt — a
-- corporation, was wound up or struck off — is owed severance as if he had
-- been dismissed.
@ref law:4
DECLARE `how the employer ended, under section 4` IS ONE OF
    `the employer died, under section 4`
    `the employer went bankrupt, under section 4`
    `the corporation was wound up or struck off, under section 4`
    `the employer did not end, under section 4`

GIVEN e IS A `how the employer ended, under section 4`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 entitles him as if he were dismissed` e IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the employer did not end, under section 4` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5`

-- (א): when an employee dies, the employer pays his survivors severance as
-- if it had dismissed him; the survivors are the spouse at the death (a
-- reputed spouse living with him included) and a child dependent on him
-- under chapter ה' of the National Insurance Law, and, where there is no
-- such spouse or child, children and parents mainly supported by him and
-- siblings who lived in his home twelve months before the death and were
-- wholly supported by him. (ב): severance owed to survivors other than the
-- spouse or a dependent child is deposited in the regional labour court,
-- which decides who takes it and in what shares. (ב1): one who died in the
-- determining period (7.10.2023 to a year after the declaration of a
-- special situation on the home front ends, which the Minister may extend
-- by up to 12 months) — his severance goes to his survivors, and where he
-- left none, to his heirs by law or by will. (ג): severance paid under the
-- section is not part of the estate.
@ref law:5
`section 5 pays the survivors of an employee who died as if he were dismissed` MEANS TRUE

DECLARE `survivor under section 5` IS ONE OF
    `the spouse at the death, a reputed spouse living with him included, under section 5`
    `a child dependent on him under the National Insurance Law, under section 5`
    `a child or a parent mainly supported by him, under section 5`
    `a sibling who lived in his home twelve months and was wholly supported by him, under section 5`
    `someone else, under section 5`

GIVEN s IS A `survivor under section 5`
      `he left a spouse or a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 makes a survivor of` s `he left a spouse or a dependent child` IF
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `the spouse at the death, a reputed spouse living with him included, under section 5` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a child dependent on him under the National Insurance Law, under section 5` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a child or a parent mainly supported by him, under section 5` THEN NOT `he left a spouse or a dependent child`
    WHEN `a sibling who lived in his home twelve months and was wholly supported by him, under section 5` THEN NOT `he left a spouse or a dependent child`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN s IS A `survivor under section 5`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5(ב) deposits the severance in the regional labour court for` s IF
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `the spouse at the death, a reputed spouse living with him included, under section 5` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a child dependent on him under the National Insurance Law, under section 5` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `someone else, under section 5` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `he died in the determining period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he left a survivor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5(ב1) pays his heirs by law or by will` `he died in the determining period` `he left a survivor` IF
    `he died in the determining period` AND (NOT `he left a survivor`)

`severance paid under section 5 is part of the estate` MEANS FALSE

§§ `6`

-- An employee who resigned for his own health or a family member's, where
-- the medical findings, the conditions of work and the rest of the
-- circumstances gave sufficient cause, has resigned as one dismissed. Who is
-- a family member, the regulations set.
@ref law:6
GIVEN `resigned for his health or a family member's` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the findings, the conditions of work and the rest gave sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6 counts the resignation as a dismissal` `resigned for his health or a family member's` `the findings, the conditions of work and the rest gave sufficient cause` IF
    `resigned for his health or a family member's` AND `the findings, the conditions of work and the rest gave sufficient cause`

`who is a family member under section 6` MEANS
    `set elsewhere` "שר העבודה, בתקנות פיצויי פיטורים (חישוב הפיצויים והתפטרות שרואים אותה כפיטורים), התשכ\"ד-1964, באישור ועדת העבודה של הכנסת"

§§ `7`

-- (א): a woman who resigned within nine months of giving birth, to care
-- for the child, has resigned as one dismissed; so has one who (1) adopted
-- a child under 13 and told her employer, (2) received a child in custody
-- as an intended parent under the surrogacy law, or (3) received into her
-- home as a foster parent a child of ten or less, with the foster
-- supervisor's approval that the child's good asked it — each resigning to
-- care for the child within nine months of receiving it. (ב): so has a
-- man, where (1) his spouse was employed six consecutive months just
-- before his resignation, (2) the child is in his sole custody, or in his
-- sole care for his spouse's disability or illness, or (3) his spouse was
-- self-employed twelve consecutive months just before the birth or the
-- receiving and did not stop to care for the child. (ג): where one spouse
-- resigned on this ground, the other cannot. (ד)–(ה): the notices and the
-- proof of self-employment are the Minister's to set.
@ref law:7
DECLARE `how the child came, under section 7` IS ONE OF
    `born to her, under section 7`
    `adopted, under section 7`
    `received as an intended parent under the surrogacy law, under section 7`
    `received as a foster parent, under section 7`

@desc The facts §7 asks about a parent who resigned.
DECLARE `a parent's resignation under section 7` HAS
    `how the child came`                                IS A `how the child came, under section 7`
    `months from the birth or the receiving`            IS A NUMBER @desc to the resignation
    `the child's age in years when received`            IS A NUMBER @desc for an adopted or a foster child
    `told the employer of the adoption`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the foster supervisor approved it for the child's good` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resigned to care for the child`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the father`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `his spouse was employed six consecutive months just before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child is in his sole custody or sole care`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc in his sole care for his spouse's disability or illness
    `his spouse was self-employed twelve consecutive months before and did not stop` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other spouse resigned on this ground`          IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN r IS A `a parent's resignation under section 7`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7(א) reaches how the child came` r IF
    CONSIDER r's `how the child came`
    WHEN `born to her, under section 7` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adopted, under section 7` THEN
        r's `the child's age in years when received` LESS THAN 13 AND r's `told the employer of the adoption`
    WHEN `received as an intended parent under the surrogacy law, under section 7` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `received as a foster parent, under section 7` THEN
        r's `the child's age in years when received` AT MOST 10 AND r's `the foster supervisor approved it for the child's good`

GIVEN r IS A `a parent's resignation under section 7`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7 counts a parent's resignation as a dismissal` r IF
        r's `resigned to care for the child`
    AND r's `months from the birth or the receiving` AT MOST 9
    AND `section 7(א) reaches how the child came` r
    AND (NOT r's `the other spouse resigned on this ground`)
    AND (    (NOT r's `is the father`)
         OR r's `his spouse was employed six consecutive months just before`
         OR r's `the child is in his sole custody or sole care`
         OR r's `his spouse was self-employed twelve consecutive months before and did not stop`)

`a mother of a child adopted at three, resigning five months after` MEANS
    `a parent's resignation under section 7` WITH
        `how the child came`                                IS `adopted, under section 7`
        `months from the birth or the receiving`            IS 5
        `the child's age in years when received`            IS 3
        `told the employer of the adoption`                 IS TRUE
        `the foster supervisor approved it for the child's good` IS FALSE
        `resigned to care for the child`                    IS TRUE
        `is the father`                                     IS FALSE
        `his spouse was employed six consecutive months just before` IS FALSE
        `the child is in his sole custody or sole care`     IS FALSE
        `his spouse was self-employed twelve consecutive months before and did not stop` IS FALSE
        `the other spouse resigned on this ground`          IS FALSE

#ASSERT `section 7 counts a parent's resignation as a dismissal` `a mother of a child adopted at three, resigning five months after`

§§ `8`

-- A resignation because the employee moved home is a dismissal where he
-- moved (1) on his marriage, to the town in Israel his spouse lived in, (2)
-- to an agricultural town from one that is not, or to a town in a
-- development area from one that is not, or (3) for another reason the
-- regulations set as justifying the move — each in the conditions the
-- regulations set, as they set which towns are agricultural or in a
-- development area. Set elsewhere: whether the conditions are met is an
-- input.
@ref law:8
DECLARE `move of home under section 8` IS ONE OF
    `on marriage, to the spouse's town in Israel, under section 8`
    `to an agricultural town or a development area, under section 8`
    `for another reason the regulations set, under section 8`
    `no move section 8 names, under section 8`

GIVEN m IS A `move of home under section 8`
      `the conditions the regulations set are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8 counts the resignation as a dismissal` m `the conditions the regulations set are met` IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `no move section 8 names, under section 8` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `the conditions the regulations set are met`

`the conditions section 8 sends to the regulations` MEANS
    `set elsewhere` "שר העבודה, בתקנות פיצויי פיטורים (חישוב הפיצויים והתפטרות שרואים אותה כפיטורים), התשכ\"ד-1964, באישור ועדת העבודה של הכנסת"

§§ `9`

-- (א): an employee on a contract for a fixed term that came to its end is
-- as one dismissed, unless the employer offered to renew it; one who
-- refused the renewal is as one who resigned. (ב): the offer is given at
-- least three months before the term ends — one given later is not the
-- offer (א) speaks of.
@ref law:9
GIVEN `the fixed term came to its end` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer offered to renew it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months before the end the offer was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9 counts the end of the term as a dismissal` `the fixed term came to its end` `the employer offered to renew it` `months before the end the offer was given` IF
        `the fixed term came to its end`
    AND (NOT (`the employer offered to renew it` AND `months before the end the offer was given` AT LEAST 3))

#ASSERT `section 9 counts the end of the term as a dismissal` TRUE TRUE 2
#ASSERT NOT `section 9 counts the end of the term as a dismissal` TRUE TRUE 3

§§ `11`

-- (א): a resignation for a material worsening of the conditions of work,
-- or for other circumstances of the relationship in which he cannot be
-- asked to go on, is a dismissal. (ב): so is a seasonal worker's, after
-- three consecutive seasons at the workplace, for not being assured
-- continuous work there. (ג): so is one made just before, and because of,
-- (1) enlisting in regular military service, (2) beginning civil service,
-- (4) volunteer service that deferred his regular service, or (5)
-- national-civil service — (2), (4) and (5) once he served six months; (3)
-- was struck out. (ד): so is one for election as a salaried head or deputy
-- head of a local authority, unless the employer agreed in writing that
-- the term counts as unpaid leave. (ה): so is one made after reaching the
-- retirement age the Retirement Age Law, 2004, sets — and what a provident
-- fund pays him out of the employer's contributions meant as or in place
-- of severance may be set off against it, even without §§14 or 20. (ו): so
-- is one made while the law on the families of fallen soldiers bars his
-- dismissal.
@ref law:11
DECLARE `service a resignation comes before, under section 11(ג)` IS ONE OF
    `regular military service, under section 11(ג)`
    `civil service, under section 11(ג)`
    `volunteer service that deferred regular service, under section 11(ג)`
    `national-civil service, under section 11(ג)`
    `no service section 11(ג) names, under section 11(ג)`

@desc The facts §11 asks about a resignation.
DECLARE `a resignation under section 11` HAS
    `a material worsening, or circumstances in which he cannot be asked to go on` IS A BOOLEAN
    `seasonal, after three consecutive seasons, continuous work not assured` IS A BOOLEAN
    `just before and because of`                     IS A `service a resignation comes before, under section 11(ג)`
    `months served in it`                            IS A NUMBER
    `elected a salaried head or deputy head of a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer agreed in writing the term is unpaid leave` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `the retirement age the Retirement Age Law sets for him` IS A NUMBER @desc חוק גיל פרישה, התשס"ד-2004, §3 and its schedule: 67 for a man, 65 for a woman, lower by the month of birth for the years of transition; outside the pinned sections, an input
    `while the fallen soldiers' families law bars his dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN r IS A `a resignation under section 11`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11(ג) counts the resignation before the service` r IF
    CONSIDER r's `just before and because of`
    WHEN `regular military service, under section 11(ג)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `no service section 11(ג) names, under section 11(ג)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE r's `months served in it` AT LEAST 6

GIVEN r IS A `a resignation under section 11`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11(ה) counts the resignation at the retirement age` r IF
    r's `age` AT LEAST r's `the retirement age the Retirement Age Law sets for him`

GIVEN r IS A `a resignation under section 11`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11 counts the resignation as a dismissal` r IF
        r's `a material worsening, or circumstances in which he cannot be asked to go on`
    OR  r's `seasonal, after three consecutive seasons, continuous work not assured`
    OR  `section 11(ג) counts the resignation before the service` r
    OR  (r's `elected a salaried head or deputy head of a local authority` AND (NOT r's `the employer agreed in writing the term is unpaid leave`))
    OR  `section 11(ה) counts the resignation at the retirement age` r
    OR  r's `while the fallen soldiers' families law bars his dismissal`

GIVEN `the severance owed` IS A NUMBER
      `paid by a provident fund out of the employer's contributions meant for severance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the severance left for the employer under section 11(ה)` `the severance owed` `paid by a provident fund out of the employer's contributions meant for severance` IS
    max 0 (`the severance owed` MINUS `paid by a provident fund out of the employer's contributions meant for severance`)

#ASSERT `the severance left for the employer under section 11(ה)` 100000 70000 EQUALS 30000

§§ `11א`

-- One who resigned to enlist in the police or the prison service, just
-- before enlisting, is owed severance — he or his survivors — where (1) he
-- served six months at least, (2) his service ended on a ground that earns
-- severance under this law, or (3) it ended because he was found unsuited,
-- unless in circumstances that would not have earned him police or prison
-- retirement pay.
@ref law:11א
GIVEN `resigned to enlist in the police or the prison service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months served there` IS A NUMBER
      `the service ended on a ground that earns severance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it ended as unsuited, in circumstances that would earn retirement pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11א entitles the recruit or his survivors` `resigned to enlist in the police or the prison service` `months served there` `the service ended on a ground that earns severance` `it ended as unsuited, in circumstances that would earn retirement pay` IF
        `resigned to enlist in the police or the prison service`
    AND (   `months served there` AT LEAST 6
         OR `the service ended on a ground that earns severance`
         OR `it ended as unsuited, in circumstances that would earn retirement pay`)

§§ `12`

-- (א): one month's wage for each year of work for a salaried employee
-- (paid mainly by the month or a longer period), two weeks' wage for each
-- year for one paid by the day or the hour; a part of a year after a full
-- one in proportion (for a seasonal worker, a part of a year in proportion
-- even if his periods do not make up a year). (ב): the Minister may raise
-- the rate for wage-earners by regulations — set elsewhere, an input.
@ref law:12
DECLARE `how the employee is paid under section 12` IS ONE OF
    `salaried, by the month or longer, under section 12`
    `a wage-earner, by the day or the hour, under section 12`

-- What a month's and what two weeks' wage are is the regulations' (§13),
-- so the wage of the period §12 counts is an input, found for the kind of
-- employee he is.
GIVEN p IS A `how the employee is paid under section 12`
      `the wage of the period section 12 counts` IS A NUMBER @desc one month's wage for one salaried, two weeks' wage for a wage-earner, as the regulations under §13 find it
      `years of work` IS A NUMBER @desc a part of a year as a fraction
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `severance pay under section 12` p `the wage of the period section 12 counts` `years of work` IS
    `the wage of the period section 12 counts` TIMES `years of work`

#ASSERT `severance pay under section 12` `salaried, by the month or longer, under section 12` 10000 2.5 EQUALS 25000

§§ `13`

-- The Minister of Labour sets by regulations which components of the whole
-- wage count, how the wage severance is computed on is found, and which
-- breaks in work do not count; set elsewhere (the law's own gap above), so
-- the month's wage is an input of every rule here.
@ref law:13
`the wage section 13 sends to the regulations` MEANS `why the Severance Pay Law's sections state no wage`

§§ `13ב`

-- Notwithstanding §13, the wage severance is computed on is no less than
-- the minimum wage as §1 of the Minimum Wage Law defines it, in proportion
-- to the position (l4/laws/minimum-wage-law.l4).
@ref law:13ב
GIVEN `the wage by the regulations` IS A NUMBER
      `the monthly minimum wage` IS A NUMBER @desc as the Minister publishes it under §6 of the Minimum Wage Law; an input
      `the share of a full position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the wage severance is computed on under section 13ב` `the wage by the regulations` `the monthly minimum wage` `the share of a full position` IS
    max `the wage by the regulations`
        (`the minimum wage owed for the month under section 2` `the monthly minimum wage` `the share of a full position` 0)

#ASSERT `the wage severance is computed on under section 13ב` 2000 5880.02 0.5 EQUALS 2940.01
#ASSERT `the wage severance is computed on under section 13ב` 9000 5880.02 1 EQUALS 9000

§§ `14`

-- A payment to a provident fund, a pension fund or the like takes the place
-- of severance pay only where the collective agreement that applies to the
-- employer and the employee says so, and to the extent it says so, or
-- where the Minister of Labour approved it, and to the extent approved. Of
-- the two, the larger extent governs: either is a ground of its own (the
-- reading taken here). What is not taken the place of, the employer owes.
-- The Minister's general approval is set elsewhere: its share is an input.
@ref law:14
GIVEN `the share the collective agreement sets` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 where the agreement sets none
      `the share the Minister approved` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 where no approval applies; the general approval is set elsewhere
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of severance a fund payment takes the place of under section 14` `the share the collective agreement sets` `the share the Minister approved` IS
    min 1 (max `the share the collective agreement sets` `the share the Minister approved`)

GIVEN `the severance` IS A NUMBER, `the share taken the place of` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the severance the employer still owes under section 14` `the severance` `the share taken the place of` IS
    `the severance` TIMES (1 MINUS `the share taken the place of`)

#ASSERT `the share of severance a fund payment takes the place of under section 14` (72%) 0 EQUALS 72%
#ASSERT `the share of severance a fund payment takes the place of under section 14` 0 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the severance the employer still owes under section 14` 100000 (72%) EQUALS 28000
#ASSERT `the severance the employer still owes under section 14` 100000 1 EQUALS 0

§§ `15`

-- An employee, or his survivor, entitled by an enactment to a pension from
-- the employer on his retirement or for another reason, has the pension in
-- place of his right to severance under this law.
@ref law:15
GIVEN `entitled by an enactment to a pension from the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the severance under this law` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the severance owed beside a pension under section 15` `entitled by an enactment to a pension from the employer` `the severance under this law` IS
    IF `entitled by an enactment to a pension from the employer` THEN 0 ELSE `the severance under this law`

#ASSERT `the severance owed beside a pension under section 15` TRUE 50000 EQUALS 0

§§ `16`

-- An employee dismissed in circumstances that the collective agreement
-- that applies to the employer and the employee — and, where there is
-- none, the one that applies to the most employees of the branch — says
-- justify a dismissal without severance, or with part of it, is owed
-- none, or that part. What the agreement says is an input.
@ref law:16
GIVEN `the collective agreement justifies dismissal without full severance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share of the severance it leaves` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 where it justifies none at all
      `the severance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the severance owed under section 16` `the collective agreement justifies dismissal without full severance` `the share of the severance it leaves` `the severance` IS
    IF `the collective agreement justifies dismissal without full severance`
    THEN `the share of the severance it leaves` TIMES `the severance`
    ELSE `the severance`

GIVEN `the collective agreement justifies dismissal without full severance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 16 lets the severance be denied or cut` `the collective agreement justifies dismissal without full severance` IF
    `the collective agreement justifies dismissal without full severance`

#ASSERT `the severance owed under section 16` TRUE 0.5 80000 EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `the severance owed under section 16` FALSE 0 80000 EQUALS 80000

§§ `29`

-- A compromise on severance, and a release, have no effect unless made in
-- writing and saying expressly that they are about severance.
@ref law:29
GIVEN `made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it says expressly it is about severance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a compromise or a release has effect under section 29` `made in writing` `it says expressly it is about severance` IF
    `made in writing` AND `it says expressly it is about severance`

#ASSERT NOT `a compromise or a release has effect under section 29` TRUE FALSE

§§ `30`

-- (א): for this law, the State is an employer like any other. (ב): for the
-- police and the prison service, §§2(6), 8 and 17 do not apply, §3 does
-- not reach a dismissal under their ordinances, a change made by their
-- authority is no worsening under §11, and their rules of service stand
-- for §16's collective agreement — none of which reaches a teacher.
@ref law:30
`the Severance Pay Law binds the State as an employer` MEANS TRUE

`section 30(ב) reaches only the police and the prison service` MEANS TRUE

§§ `31`

-- (א): the law takes from no right an employee has under a law, a
-- collective agreement or a contract — and, for §12, under custom — and
-- does not exhaust his rights in any negotiation on retirement: of the
-- law's severance and another source's, he has the larger. (ב): being owed
-- severance takes nothing from his rights that depend on seniority.
@ref law:31
GIVEN `what the Severance Pay Law gives` IS A NUMBER, `what another source gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what governs between the Severance Pay Law and another source` `what the Severance Pay Law gives` `what another source gives` IS
    max `what the Severance Pay Law gives` `what another source gives`

`severance takes from a right that depends on seniority` MEANS FALSE

#ASSERT `what governs between the Severance Pay Law and another source` 25000 20000 EQUALS 25000
#ASSERT NOT `severance takes from a right that depends on seniority`
